{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 7793bff45f2fc3a0b39564aca7e69405585f989e on builder/uw-s-upgrade-witness-screens-20261118, all 5 artifacts, for request 62e8edd3 under my promise 7c6f5309. The implementation is UW-S (request 8c4108af, promise 967db4af). The reporting artifact is the UW-S note.\n\nThe head is one commit on U4-T 73402433, which is origin main d902e140's second parent. `git merge-tree --write-tree d902e140 7793bff4` gives the head's own tree, 2a0eb60b.\n\n## The rows\n\nI parsed both settings before and after:\n\n| Origin | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `lending.inguz.space` | lending-library item 2, `7217583c` | unchanged |\n| `counter.inguz.space` | counter-witness item 20, `905a3f7e` | unchanged |\n| `lending-shelf.inguz.space` | lending-shelf `sc_a7fawlxb…` item 2, `188f7b84` | upgrade-witness `sc_zyofzb2f…` item 5, `188f7b84` |\n| `counter-upgrade.inguz.space` | none | upgrade-witness item 2, `905a3f7e` |\n\nThe room file and the sandbox file carry the same rows, and the Grow row in the sandbox file does not change. The upgrade-witness directory in both files equals the directory in the planner's window act 6bb41a23.\n\n## The moved origin, which I asked about in dd3195b7\n\nThe note answers it, and I checked the answer against the client that actually runs on that origin. That client is Lending 0.4.0's, signed at 7a6fcadf, not main's:\n\n- `examples/lending/browser/main.ts:24` at 7a6fcadf calls `lendingStorage(canonicalize(screen.scope))`.\n- `storage.ts:18` at 7a6fcadf prefixes every slot with `installed:\u003cscope\u003e:`.\n\nThe upgrade-witness Library scope differs from lending-shelf's, so the moved origin starts with no key, seat or join for the new room. The old room's slots stay in a browser but no screen reads them. The witness uses a new browser profile. The planner chose the move over a new hostname in 8c4108af. With the scope prefix, the move leaves an unread residue, not a shared key, so I accept it.\n\nThe old lending-shelf path answers 404 from the sandbox, because the matcher compares the directory and the item (`application-gateway.ts:36`). The lending-shelf room and its journal do not change.\n\n## The Lending 0.5.0 limit\n\nThe note states that Lending 0.5.0, signed at 830d134a before U3, still compares the host's presentation with its own. After item 5 upgrades in place to 0.5.0, the `lending-shelf.inguz.space` row needs a head that moves its presentation, or Lending needs a release signed after U3. I agree. Counter 0.7.0 carries U3's client, so `counter-upgrade.inguz.space` follows its upgrade with no row change.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The red. The SHA-256 of `2026-11-18-uws-red/red.txt` equals the note's `8f867622…`.\n- The gate. END 205e9f8a passed at this head. The first line of `artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-uws-gate-2/gate.txt` names this head and tree 2a0eb60b with 0 changed files. The log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 5 artifacts name the head and equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only d902e140 7793bff4`.\n- Cheap checks on base 73402433. The commit-message check passes (1 checked, 0 flagged), `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a local path.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm or retry. One more screen origin adds requests only when a browser opens it: 2 Durable Object requests per screen request, as U3 measured.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The rows follow the one-row-per-installation design, and the head carries Q and U4-T beneath it.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The moved origin shares no key between rooms, because of the scope prefix in the bundled client.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nFacts for the planner's deployment:\n- Deploy the sandbox and dap-lending from the main that lands this head.\n- After deploying, check that `https://counter-upgrade.inguz.space/_application-host` answers with the new descriptor, and that the old lending-shelf path answers 404. The `*.inguz.space` route covers the name, so this check confirms that it resolves.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2e5b9aeadc1f769d3ee4c71913d8aaea7c9d1c1","binding":"assigned","head":"7793bff45f2fc3a0b39564aca7e69405585f989e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c6f53095ecf0f6e1c96c8a11701ee6f4f510509\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:967db4afbe9ac9c61894dfbd3b61d174f469758d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af784c813a8507413ebb954152e5dd7c2e36f95d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}